      "impact": "The POT and TACH signals will be pulled to VCC (likely 12V), exceeding the ATtiny's absolute maximum voltage and causing damage or incorrect readings.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["U3"],
      "pins": ["U3.6", "U3.5", "U3.3", "U3.4", "U3.1"],
      "nets": ["PWM", "SDA", "POT", "TACH", "RST"],
      "observed": "Two microcontrollers are present: U2 (ATtiny45-20P) and U3 (ATtiny13V-10S). Both are connected to the same signal nets: PWM (U2.5, U3.6), SDA (U2.4, U3.5), POT (U2.6, U3.3), TACH (U2.7, U3.4), RST (U2.1, U3.1).",
      "expected": "A single ATtiny microcontroller as described in the specification ('an ATtiny-driven fan controller'). The extra microcontroller will cause bus contention on shared nets if both are populated.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Atmel/ ... an ATtiny-driven fan controller"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U2 ATtiny45-20P and U3 ATtiny13V-10S both present and connected to PWM, SDA, POT, TACH, RST"}
      ],
      "impact": "If both U2 and U3 are populated, they will drive the same nets (PWM, SDA) causing contention and likely preventing the board from functioning.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["C2"],
      "pins": ["C2.1", "C2.2"],
      "nets": ["VCC", "+5V", "GND"],
      "observed": "Two capacitors are both labeled C2. One 100nF capacitor is connected between VCC and GND. Another 100nF capacitor is connected between +5V and GND.",
      "expected": "Each component should have a unique reference designator. The duplicate reference will cause BOM and assembly errors.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "C2 100nF on VCC (first image, top right)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "C2 100nF on +5V (second image, near U1)"}
      ],
      "impact": "Assembly house may place only one capacitor or misplace components, leading to missing decoupling or incorrect net connections.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains multiple anomalies: pull-up resistors R3 and R6 are tied to VCC instead of the ATtiny's +5V rail, exposing the MCU to excessive voltage; an extra ATtiny (U3) is present and shares nets with U2, risking contention; and capacitor C2 is duplicated. These deviations would likely cause malfunction or damage."
}

